From 42978cf76fb520f8dfb8dcdac03ab7f26392fd80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Venkatakrishnaiah Pari <vpari@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 13:37:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ksync_fence: drop removed signal_on_any arg from
 dma_fence_array_create()

Upstream dropped the signal_on_any parameter from
dma_fence_array_create()/dma_fence_array_init() (commit
"dma-buf/dma_fence_array: remove unused functionality v4"). Match the
new 4-argument signature. Note: WAIT_ANY semantics in
ksync_wait_multiple() are no longer honored by the fence array itself
since the kernel dropped early-signal-on-any support.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ia3967e53562280f30c9738a14f8c0598fae3c71f
---
 src/ksync_fence.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ksync_fence.c b/src/ksync_fence.c
index 896c41b..2787547 100644
--- a/src/ksync_fence.c
+++ b/src/ksync_fence.c
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ static struct dma_fence *ksync_fence_array_create(
 	}
 
 	array = dma_fence_array_create(count, fences,
-			dma_fence_context_alloc(1), 0, any);
+			dma_fence_context_alloc(1), 0);
 	if (array)
 		out_fence = &array->base;
 	else
-- 
2.43.0
